; --- Furniture ----------------------------------------------------------------
; Transforms below were solved once by a throwaway fit probe (target size +
; target world position + yaw) and baked here, per the project's "author in the
; .tscn" convention. The downloads arrive at wildly different scales — the fan
; and trash can are ~450 units across and offset hundreds of units from their
; own origin — so none of these numbers are guessable by hand.
[node name="Furniture" type="Node3D" parent="."]

; Every piece below was split out and squared up in Blender
; (Tools note: /tmp straighten pass, 2026-07-28). The downloads are staged
; product shots — the bed, desk and chair were one inseparable mesh, and the two
; bookcases sat at ~30 deg to each other — so nothing could be aligned to a wall
; as shipped. Each is now its own GLB, axis-aligned, origin at base-centre, which
; is why the transforms here are plain position + scale with no stray rotations.

; Head to the north wall, east side. Model is 2.25 m across including the duvet
; overhang; 0.667 brings that to a 1.5 m double.
;
; The bedding was green. This is ONE mesh with ONE surface and ONE 1024 atlas —
; 54% brown wood frame, 17% green duvet, 25% desaturated sheets — so it cannot be
; re-skinned with a flat colour without recolouring the frame too, and a material
; tint cannot change a hue at all (albedo_color multiplies: green times cream is
; muddy green). Tools/recolour_texture.py rewrites just the green hue band of
; bed_Image_1.png in HSV, keeping V so every fold and shadow survives. The
; untouched original is kept beside it as bed_Image_1_source.png, which is what
; the tool reads, so the colour can be redone without re-downloading.
[node name="Bed" parent="Furniture" instance=ExtResource("12_bed")]
transform = Transform3D(0.667, 0, 0, 0, 0.667, 0, 0, 0, 0.667, 2.31, 0, -1.11)

; Desk built from primitives rather than downloaded. The set's desk could not be
; separated from its chair — every split left the two joined, so min-area
; bounding-box straightening aligned to the pair's L-shape instead of the desk,
; and it stayed ~20 deg off no matter what. Boxes are square by construction,
; cost nothing, and follow test_scene_builder.gd's _build_table() idiom.
[node name="Desk" type="Node3D" parent="Furniture"]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, -0.95, 0, -1.78)

[node name="Top" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="Furniture/Desk"]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0.73, 0)
mesh = SubResource("Mesh_desk_top")
surface_material_override/0 = SubResource("Mat_desk")

[node name="SideL" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="Furniture/Desk"]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, -0.655, 0.355, 0)
mesh = SubResource("Mesh_desk_side")
surface_material_override/0 = SubResource("Mat_desk")

[node name="SideR" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="Furniture/Desk"]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0.655, 0.355, 0)
mesh = SubResource("Mesh_desk_side")
surface_material_override/0 = SubResource("Mat_desk")

[node name="BackRail" type="MeshInstance3D" parent="Furniture/Desk"]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0.64, -0.29)
mesh = SubResource("Mesh_desk_rail")
surface_material_override/0 = SubResource("Mat_desk")

; Dropped 0.12 on Y. The GLB is not zeroed to its base — its geometry starts at
; y +0.12 in local space — so at y 0 both cases hovered 12 cm above the carpet
; with daylight under the plinths. Their colliders were already floor-to-1.8 and
; now agree with the meshes.
;
; Yaw 90, so the shelves face EAST into the room. The model's open face is +Z
; and its solid back -Z (checked by rendering it from all four sides); the first
; pass had them turned into the west wall showing their backs.
; Swivel desk chair, its own front is +Z (checked by rendering the model from all
; four sides before placing it). Scaled 1.25 — the download is only 0.66 m to the
; top of the backrest.
;
; Pushed out to the desk's EAST end and angled, rather than squared up in the
; middle. Centred it walled off the desk: the chair plus the player capsule's own
; 0.2 m radius blocked x -1.45..-0.45 for a metre of depth, which is the entire
; desk frontage, so the monitor could not be reached from the front at all. The
; player body is a full-height capsule and can never pass under a desk, so there
; is no arrangement where a chair squared up to a desk leaves it usable.
[node name="Chair" parent="Furniture" instance=ExtResource("20_chair")]
transform = Transform3D(-1.1746, 0, -0.4275, 0, 1.25, 0, 0.4275, 0, -1.1746, -0.3, 0, -1.2)

; Two of the tall bookcase rather than the set's small one, which carries a
; corner return that defeats the same straightening pass.
[node name="BookcaseA" parent="Furniture" instance=ExtResource("17_bctall")]
transform = Transform3D(0, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, -1, 0, 0, -2.345, -0.12, -1.55)

[node name="BookcaseB" parent="Furniture" instance=ExtResource("17_bctall")]
transform = Transform3D(0, 0, 1, 0, 1, 0, -1, 0, 0, -2.345, -0.12, -0.55)

; Yaw 225 deg, not 45: the model faces +Z, so 45 pointed the doors and the open
; AV bay INTO the corner and presented its back to the room.
[node name="TVStand" parent="Furniture" instance=ExtResource("15_tvstand")]
; Scaled 0.77877, down from 0.94228. True vertex extents put it at
; 1.12 x 0.97 x 1.12: the footprint is right for a corner unit but 0.97 m tall
; is a sideboard, and a 14 in set on top looked lost. Uniform 0.826 brings it to
; 0.93 x 0.80 x 0.93. Height is the only thing wrong, but the mouldings and the
; arched door panels will not take a non-uniform squash, so the footprint comes
; down with it.
;
; Position re-solved from TRUE VERTEX extents, not the AABB: at 45 deg the AABB
; of a rotated AABB inflates by up to sqrt(2), which reads as a 0.55 m gap that
; is not there. Back faces land exactly on x 2.525 and z 2.125.
transform = Transform3D(-0.55068, 0, -0.55068, 0, 0.77877, 0, 0.55068, 0, -0.55068, 2.1248, 0.0324, 1.7441)

; The functional TrashCan scene, not the bare model — it is an XRToolsPickable,
; so it can be picked up and it deletes what you drop in it. y = 0.18 puts the
; body origin (the can's centre) a half-height off the floor.
[node name="TrashCan" parent="Furniture" instance=ExtResource("16_trash")]
transform = Transform3D(1, 0, 0, 0, 1, 0, 0, 0, 1, -2.24, 0.18, 0.45)

; Bedside cabinet, back to the north wall in the gap between the bed's west edge
; (x = 1.0) and the desk. Its drawer-and-door face is the model's +X, so the yaw
; of -90 turns that to face south down the room; the door hangs ajar as shipped
; and swings into free floor. Scale 0.0826 makes it 0.62 m tall on a 0.352 m
; square plan — measured off the TOP SLAB, not the AABB, which the open door
; stretches 0.16 m past the carcass in +X.
[node name="Nightstand" parent="Furniture" instance=ExtResource("26_nightstand")]
transform = Transform3D(0, 0, -0.0826, 0, 0.0826, 0, 0.0826, 0, 0, 0.755, 0.619, -1.948)

; Both lamps are the same model. It arrives at real-world scale already and
; centred on its own origin, so the only work is lifting it by half its height
; onto whatever it stands on: the nightstand top at 0.62, the desk top at 0.75.
[node name="BedsideLamp" parent="Furniture" instance=ExtResource("27_lamp")]
transform = Transform3D(0.9, 0, 0, 0, 0.9, 0, 0, 0, 0.9, 0.754, 0.828, -1.925)

[node name="DeskLamp" parent="Furniture" instance=ExtResource("27_lamp")]
transform = Transform3D(0.9, 0, 0, 0, 0.9, 0, 0, 0, 0.9, -0.45, 0.958, -1.78)

; Light switch, west wall, on the north side of the door opening (which spans
; z 0.72 to 1.68) at the standard 1.2 m. The root is UNSCALED and yawed so its
; local +Z is out of the wall — the plate GLB carries the 0.0345 scale on its own
; child transform, which keeps the VRButton below in plain metres.
[node name="LightSwitch" type="Node3D" parent="Furniture"]
