; --- Soft props -------------------------------------------------------------
; Five floor cushions RINGING the rug (x -1.4..1.0, z -0.8..0.9), each overlapping
; its edge and yawed off-axis so they read as floor seating around it. The first
; pass put them at arbitrary spots unrelated to the rug and it read as litter.
; Scaled 0.85 across and SQUASHED to 0.45 on Y. Rendering the asset alone on a
; floor plane showed what it really is: a pair of sofa throw pillows modelled
; plump and propped upright against each other. There is no rotation that lays one
; flat — sweeping rotX only ever made the bounding box TALLER, because they are
; already resting as low as they get. At full height they read as pointed
; teardrops standing on the carpet. A non-uniform squash is the fix, and a soft
; object takes it where the wardrobe's mouldings never could: no straight lines to
; distort, and a compressed crease is what a floor cushion under weight looks
; like anyway. Each instance
; hides one of the GLB's two pillows and re-skins the other, so one 6.4k-tri
; download gives a varied scatter — the pattern mesh_filter.gd exists for.
;
; NO COLLIDERS, deliberately. XRToolsPlayerBody is a full-height capsule, so a
; 0.45 m cushion would block it outright and these sit in the open floor where
; the player walks. Walking through a cushion is the lesser wrong, and nothing
; rests on them, which is what the FurnitureCollision colliders are actually for.
[node name="SoftProps" type="Node3D" parent="."]
[node name="CushionA" type="Node3D" parent="SoftProps"]
transform = Transform3D(0.821015, 0, 0.21998, 0, 0.45, 0, -0.21998, 0, 0.821015, -1.45, 0, -0.15)
script = ExtResource("11_meshfilter")
hide_meshes = PackedStringArray("throw_pillows_01_pillow01")
skin = SubResource("Mat_cushion_cream")

[node name="Pillows" parent="SoftProps/CushionA" instance=ExtResource("37_pillows")]

[node name="CushionB" type="Node3D" parent="SoftProps"]
